    {
      "vulnerability_id": "CVE-2026-14456",
      "package": "libssl3t64",
      "installed_version": "3.5.6-1~deb13u2",
      "severity": "High",
      "status": "accepted_risk",
      "owner": "@jeremi",
      "rationale": "Debian marks the Trixie issue postponed with no fixed Trixie version, and Grype reports it wont-fix. The advisory is an unbounded pending-connection queue in the OpenSSL QUIC server path. The official v0.25.0 Linux AMD64 Relay candidate links no OpenSSL library: the reviewed binary declares only libgcc_s.so.1, libm.so.6, libc.so.6, and the program interpreter as NEEDED, contains no libssl.so.3 or libcrypto.so.3 name to load dynamically, and terminates TLS with rustls and aws-lc-rs rather than OpenSSL. libssl3t64 ships in the pinned distroless base and no image process opens it. A candidate must retain the complete ordered reference rootfs layers, which pin every libssl3t64 byte, the production OCI process contract, and the Syft-bound reviewed file digests.",
